        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "The volcanic South Shetland Islands are often windy and shrouded in mist. Mosses, lichens and flowering plants grow here, and the islands are home to gentoo and chinstrap penguins and southern giant petrels.\n\nOne option is Deception Island, where the ship passes through the narrow entrance at Neptune’s Bellows into a flooded caldera. Near the abandoned whaling station, you can see thousands of Cape petrels, along with gulls, brown and south polar skuas, and Antarctic terns. A walk through the volcanic landscape may also be possible. An alternative is to visit Half Moon Island, where chinstrap penguins and Weddell seals can be seen ashore near Argentina’s Cámara Base. Either visit can replace the other. Conditions in the Drake Passage determine the exact time of departure for the return crossing."
    },
    {
